{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c1.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c1.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c1.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The general investment-product wording in u14 determines product scope.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c1.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.219e8fa5d2e54479fcef56c1.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"88db64f4236b5c6dd4fb98994c83e7f188b4f5718902a9049ae1d3b89bd31fd1","candidate_id":"candidate.ddabc7a87cdf49a6b9332b9395c8c3ea","controlled_language":"Selected control: general-product gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific investment product or a particular product type is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. This includes promotional linkage to a fund type or fund house. The restriction does not depend on the arrangement being a structured product or on demonstrated distraction.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["scope"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.a36852e3c6f74540866fab886da4d16b","issue.bcad9cfb701f480183b3a1aac33ba7be","issue.3e363b8ccba94de997c4eb4b